(ned PID TRACKING -- one A leg, operator 2026-08-06: "i want to track PID)
(errors when we move and stop A between -90 0 90" + 3-speed tiers: "5)
(+-90s at slow, another 5 at medium and another 5 at fast". One leg =)
(move A to the target at the given feed, then a 2 s settle so the decel)
(transient and the static hold separate cleanly in the PID logs. NO)
(probing, NO puck, NO Z moves: with tool-tip kins live the XYZ joints)
(mirror the rotation to hold the tip still -- that coupled response IS)
(the measurement. The GUI pre-checks joint excursions vs soft limits.)
(Args: #1 = target A in degrees   #2 = A feed in deg/min)
o<tcp_pidt_step> sub
  #<targa> = #1
  #<arf>   = #2

  o10 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, PID TRACK: switch to MM first - this routine is metric)
  o10 endif
  o16 if [ABS[#<targa>] GT 91]
    (abort, PID TRACK: A beyond 91 deg)
  o16 endif
  o17 if [[#<arf> LT 50] OR [#<arf> GT 1800]]
    (abort, PID TRACK: feed outside 50-1800 deg/min)
  o17 endif

  M50 P0
  G90
  G1 A#<targa> F[#<arf>]
  ; 2 s settle at the stop: the decel transient dies out and the logs get
  ; a clean static-hold window at this angle before the next leg
  G4 P2.0
  M50 P1
  (DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"ned_controls"}.tcp_pidt_point{#5423}])
o<tcp_pidt_step> endsub
M2
